    "Source samples measure distances to returned closest points. They do not certify global closest minima or continuous source-surface separation. The readback compares two closest-point implementations on saved SDK tensors and never feeds an independent candidate.",
    "Each positive incompatibility witness combines an exact original-source position certificate, outward addition of source-image and comparison budgets, and an exact point-distance predicate. By the triangle inequality, a correct globally closest candidate output preserving that source cannot also satisfy the reference returned-point comparison. A missing witness does not establish compatibility.",
    "All 780 dyadic source samples certify exactly on their original stored quadratic curves. Original query 10 uses the separately certified 1e-12 membership bound at parameter 0.53; the reference output lies strictly outside the outward 2e-6 + 1e-12 joint budget.",
    "Native construction and all requested geometry/proof/comparison tolerances remain unchanged. Default requests omit source samples and retain their previous response shape. Optional requests admit at most 65 increasing finite unit fractions per source.",
    "The raw Gordon candidate retains its independent interior mismatch. Neither the source audit nor the reference-derived readback qualifies NetworkSrf, topology, boundary continuity or performance. No proprietary implementation was inspected."
